{"content":[{"c":["BEN-GEBER"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Literally, “Geber’s son,” an official in King Solomon’s court who administered the sixth of 12 districts. Ben-geber’s area of responsibility began at Ramoth-gilead in northern Transjordan and extended north as far as Argob in Bashan (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.4.13","r":"1Kgs.4.13","rawR":"1Kgs.4.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.4.13","value":"1Kgs.4.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 4:13"},"). His identification with Geber, son of Uri (v ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.4.19","r":"1Kgs.4.19","rawR":"1Kgs.4.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.4.19","value":"1Kgs.4.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"19"},"), is debatable."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"BenGeber","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 4:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.4.13","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.4.13","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.4.13"},{"anchorText":"19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.4.19","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.4.19","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.4.19"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"e8e2f9cdf9daa71d2d4e6c31f2b3e1163cd5f83b0e0ca9da568533fec52bfb02","sourceItemName":"BenGeber","sourceItemOrder":180,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"BenGeber","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Ben-Geber","title":"Ben-Geber","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}